course: dictionary
lesson: 3017
title: Dyed: colour that soaks in
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To dye something is to change its colour with a dye, which is a coloured liquid or powder. «Dyed» is the past form of dye. «She dyed her hair purple» tells you she made her hair purple, not that she painted it on the surface.
explain: «Dyed» can also describe something that has already been coloured this way, as in «dyed wool». The words around it give the clue: if someone did something, dyed is an action word; if it sits next to a thing, like wool or a T-shirt, it describes that thing.
explain: Hyphens join words into one idea. «A dyed-in-the-wool football fan» is a fan whose love of the team never changes. Read the whole phrase, not just one word, and ask what the phrase is describing.
fact: To dye means to change the colour of something with a dye.
fact: «Dyed» is the past form of dye, and it can also be an adjective, as in «dyed wool».
fact: «Dyed-in-the-wool» means fixed and never changing in your opinions.
fact: Cotton from a plant is cleaned, spun into thread, knitted into fabric, dyed, then cut and sewn into a T-shirt.
fact: Denim for jeans is woven with «blue-dyed threads» one way and white threads the other, so the inside is paler.
exercise: «She dyed her hair purple.» What does dyed mean here? | Cut very short | Washed and dried in the sun | *Changed its colour with a dye
exercise: «A dyed-in-the-wool football fan» is someone who | Has just joined the club | Is very tired after every match | *Never changes their opinions about the team | Covers their body in wool
exercise: In «cleaned, spun into thread, knitted into fabric, dyed, cut and sewn», what comes straight after knitted? | Spun | Sewn | Planted | *Dyed
test: «Denim for jeans is woven with blue-dyed threads.» What does blue-dyed mean? | Blue because it is old and worn | Woven together into a blue pattern | Shiny and smooth | *Coloured blue with a dye
test: Which sentence shows hair that has been changed with a dye? | «The hair was cut very short.» | «Her hair blew in the wind.» | «He had brown hair from birth.» | *«She dyed her hair bright red.»
exam: Jayden says «dyed» is just a colour word, like red. Is he right? | Yes, dyed means red | Yes, dyed means wet | *No, dyed is the past of dye, an action, and it can also describe fabric like «dyed wool»
